# G120 — CD Burning App

*v2. See `cd-burner.md` for prose: session-aware capacity, FFD bin-packing,
ISO 9660 canonicalization with ~N collision suffix, absorbing-terminal FSM.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Vault Backup Burner

[backup-burner @files @disc-capacity @num-discs
    IN ORDER TO
        pack vault exports onto as few CDs as possible
        with ISO-compliant names and a finalized TOC

    @plan <- [burn[pack-files-ffd {files: @files,
                                     capacity: @disc-capacity,
                                     discs: @num-discs}]]
    #plan
        discs: @plan:discs
        overflow: @plan:overflow
        total-size: sum over @files:size-bytes

    @plan:overflow
        where count > 0
        IN ORDER TO tell the user a bigger cluster is needed
        -> "would need " + (@num-discs + 1) + " discs or more"

    for @disc-plan in @plan:discs
        @disc <- [burn[new-disc {capacity-bytes: @disc-capacity}]]
        [burn[open-session {disc: @disc}]]
            || -> @resistance:reason

        @iso-names <- {}
        for @file in @disc-plan
            @iso <- [burn[canonicalize-iso-name
                            {name: @file:name, existing: @iso-names}]]
            @iso-names <- @iso-names with @iso
            [burn[add-file {disc: @disc,
                             file: {name: @iso,
                                    size-bytes: @file:size-bytes}}]]

        [burn[finalize {disc: @disc}]]
        #ready-to-burn @disc
]

---

## Verb Surface

[burn
    new-disc               {capacity-bytes}
    open-session           {disc}                  ;; || disc-finalized, session-already-open
    add-file               {disc, file}            ;; || disc-finalized, no-open-session, not-enough-space
    close-session          {disc}                  ;; || disc-finalized, no-open-session
    finalize               {disc}                  ;; || disc-finalized
    used-bytes             {disc}
    remaining-bytes        {disc}
    pack-files-ffd         {files, capacity, discs}
    canonicalize-iso-name  {name, existing}
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: absorbing terminal state via persistent resistance

The v1 modeled `Finalized` as a phase. In Innate it's not a state
value at all — it's a resolver fact about the disc that causes
every write verb to resist:

[burn[add-file {disc: @finalized-disc, file: @any}]]
    || -> @resistance:reason    ;; "disc-finalized"

The fulfillment clause is the place to decide what "finalized" means
at the choreographic level: surface as UI warning, route to a
human for a new blank disc, or just halt.

---

## ISO name canonicalization as deterministic `where` constraint

[burn[canonicalize-iso-name {name: "report.txt", existing: {"REPORT.TXT"}}]
    where
        the result is uppercase alphanumeric + underscore only
        and the stem portion is no more than 8 characters
        and the extension is no more than 3 characters
        and if the canonical form collides with an existing name
            the stem is truncated to make room for "~N" suffix
            where N is the smallest positive integer producing no collision
]
-> "REPORT~1.TXT"

---

## Demo

[demo
    @disc <- [burn[new-disc {capacity-bytes: 700000000}]]
    [burn[open-session {disc: @disc}]]
    [burn[add-file {disc: @disc,
                     file: {name: "album1.flac", size-bytes: 100000000}}]]
    [burn[add-file {disc: @disc,
                     file: {name: "album2.flac", size-bytes: 150000000}}]]
    -> [burn[used-bytes {disc: @disc}]]         ;; -> 285000000  (250M + 35M overhead)

    [burn[close-session {disc: @disc}]]
    [burn[open-session  {disc: @disc}]]
    [burn[add-file {disc: @disc,
                     file: {name: "bonus.mp3", size-bytes: 50000000}}]]
    -> [burn[used-bytes {disc: @disc}]]         ;; -> 370000000  (2 sessions × 35M)

    [burn[finalize {disc: @disc}]]
    [burn[add-file {disc: @disc, file: @anything}]]
        || -> "disc-finalized"                    ;; -> "disc-finalized"
]
